# Force devDependencies (including every @types/* package and TypeScript
# itself) to install regardless of the calling environment's NODE_ENV.
#
# Root cause this fixes: npm's `omit` config defaults to "dev" whenever
# NODE_ENV=production is set in the environment -- a common default in many
# corporate/CI setups, and easy to have set globally without realizing it.
# Every @types/* package in this project is a devDependency, so under that
# default, `npm ci` silently installs only ~126 of the ~311 packages this
# project needs, node_modules/@types/ ends up completely empty, and
# `tsc --noEmit` fails with "Cannot find type definition file" for every
# single one -- not a random subset, all of them, which is the actual
# symptom that was reported (and reproduced) against this repository.
#
# `include=dev` is the current, non-deprecated npm config for this --
# verified to eliminate the failure under NODE_ENV=production with zero
# side effects or warnings in the normal (unaffected) case.
include=dev
